# NO TRAILING SLASH, and the slash is what let one in on 2026-09-07: a
# `node_modules/` pattern matches a DIRECTORY only, and a worktree set up
# with `ln -s ../rofl/node_modules` puts a SYMLINK of that name in the tree.
# `git add -A` took it, it rode into a merge commit, and the next checkout
# of this branch would have pointed a fresh clone's dependencies at a path
# on one laptop. Same shape as every other gate here that inherited the
# form of its first incident: the rule was written for the thing's usual
# shape rather than for its name.
node_modules
dist/
*.snapshot.json
facts/generated/

# reference material, fetched not written — see reference/kjs/PROVENANCE.md
reference/

# A household's own week: names, hours, and the intervals when a child is
# alone. Local only, never pushed. `examples/spat/week.example.rofl` is the
# made-up household the demo and the tests ship with.
examples/spat/week.rofl
examples/spat/week-sep.rofl
examples/spat/week-*.rofl
examples/spat/*.local.md
